       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up sharply. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (a more typical range)\n- **1600 mg per day in total,** for example 400 mg 4 times daily\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional. I'd suggest adding a note with your rationale, and it may be worth checking with pharmacy first."
      }
