       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose. I'm not aware of any indication that justifies it. It carries a real risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and it's too risky for me to enter on my own.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within limits.** I can enter 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day) right now. I can add a note such as \"max dose, monitor GI/renal function.\"\n- **Enter it yourself through the normal channel.** If you think this dose is warranted, you can place it directly. Pharmacy verification will probably review it, and that's a useful second check.\n- **Call pharmacy or toxicology.** If you're trying to reach a goal that standard dosing isn't meeting, they can suggest other options. Examples are adding acetaminophen, switching agents, or using adjuncts.\n\nIf you tell me what you're treating, I can help work out an alternative regimen. Or tell me the dose you want to go with and I'll enter it."
